------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Checked into this repository under web/vendor/ rather than installed:

  Rapier (@dimforge/rapier3d-compat)    web/vendor/rapier.es.js
  Copyright the Rapier contributors
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/dimforge/rapier

  This is the wasm-inline build the physics code was written against, pinned
  here so the viewport and the headless `caliper sim` harness run the same
  engine. web/vite.config.ts aliases the package name to it.

  butai keyboard protocol helpers                       web/vendor/butai/
    protocol
  Copyright the butai contributors
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
  https://github.com/dieterpl/butai

  The client half of butai's framed protocol: the custom elements that paint a
  live pane, its colour resolution and its message builders. MPL-2.0 is a
  per-file copyleft — these four files stay under it inside this repository,
  and a change to any of them has to be published under MPL-2.0 too. The rest
  of caliper is unaffected by that; Apache-2.0 applies to it as normal.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Installed dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Not vendored here; each carries its own license. Notably three.js (MIT), which
draws the viewport, and build123d (Apache-2.0), which every design is written
against. The full sets are in web/package.json and requirements.txt.
